{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/errorpresentation"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Error Presentation"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default Error placeholders do beyond showing a generic icon and message: telling a connectivity problem apart from everything else, an optional second action alongside Retry, and a user-facing message distinct from "},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Error presentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Error-presentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one state whose presentation can’t be fully generic — a timed-out request, a missing article, and a malformed response all deserve different words, and sometimes a different action, even though they’re all just an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Scr